#-
# RGW VinylCache VMOD for Vinyl Cache
#
# This VMOD provides integration between Vinyl Cache (vinyld) and RGW,
# allowing VCL to call RGW for request processing and receive responses.
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
# Author: RGW VinylCache Team

$ABI vrt
$Module rgw_vinyl 1 "RGW VinylCache Integration"

DESCRIPTION
===========

This VMOD provides a bridge between Vinyl Cache (vinyld) and RGW (RadosGW).
It allows VCL configurations to:

- Initialize RGW callback handlers
- Create request contexts for RGW processing
- Send requests to RGW and receive responses
- Access cached responses from VinylCache

The VMOD acts as an IPC bridge, forwarding requests from vinyld to the
RGW process and returning responses back to vinyld for caching.

Example VCL usage::

    vcl 4.1;

    import rgw_vinyl;

    sub vcl_init {
        # Initialize the VMOD with config path and IPC socket path
        rgw_vinyl.init("/etc/rgw/vinyl.conf",
                       "/var/run/rgw_vinyl.sock");
    }

    sub vcl_recv {
        # Create a request context
        rgw_vinyl.request req = rgw_vinyl.request();

        # Start the request with method, URI, and host
        req.start(req.method, req.url, req.host);

        # Send to RGW for processing
        if (req.send() == 0) {
            return (synth(503, "RGW unavailable"));
        }

        # If RGW processed the request, return the cached response
        return (deliver);
    }

    sub vcl_deliver {
        # Add cache status header
        if (req.rgw_vinyl.cache_hit) {
            set resp.http.X-Cache = "HIT from RGW";
        } else {
            set resp.http.X-Cache = "MISS";
        }
    }

INITIALIZATION
==============

$Function VOID .init(STRING config_path = "", STRING ipc_socket_path = "")

Initialize the VMOD with configuration path and IPC socket path.

``config_path``
    Path to the RGW VinylCache configuration file.

``ipc_socket_path``
    Path to the IPC Unix domain socket for communication with RGW.

If called without arguments, defaults will be used from environment
variables or compile-time settings.

$Function VOID .fini(VOID)

Cleanup resources allocated during initialization.

Called automatically when the VCL is discarded.

CLEANUP
=======

$Function VOID .cleanup(VOID)

Perform any necessary cleanup of resources.

REQUEST OBJECT
==============

The request object maintains state for a single RGW request.

$Object request(PRIV_TASK)

Create a new request context for RGW processing.

The PRIV_TASK parameter ensures the request object is private to each
request thread, avoiding race conditions.

Example::

    rgw_vinyl.request req = rgw_vinyl.request();

REQUEST METHODS
===============

$Method VOID .start(STRING method, STRING uri, STRING host = "")

Start a new RGW request with the given method, URI, and host.

``method``
    HTTP method (GET, PUT, POST, DELETE, etc.)

``uri``
    Request URI path and query string.

``host``
    Host header value (optional).

$Method INT .send(PRIV_TASK)

Send the request to RGW for processing via IPC.

Returns:
    - 0 on failure
    - 1 on success (response available)

The method blocks until RGW processes the request and returns the
response.

$Method STRING .get_header(STRING name)

Get a response header value by name.

``name``
    Header name (e.g., "Content-Type", "ETag").

Returns the header value or NULL if not found.

$Method INT .cache_hit(VOID)

Check if the response was served from cache.

Returns:
    - 0 if cache miss
    - 1 if cache hit

$Method VOID .free(VOID)

Free resources associated with the request object.

Called automatically when the request object goes out of scope.

CACHE CONTROL
=============

$Function INT .cache_lookup(STRING key)

Check if a response is cached for the given key.

``key``
    Cache key (typically URI).

Returns:
    - 0 if not cached
    - 1 if cached

$Function INT .cache_invalidate(STRING key)

Invalidate a cached response.

``key``
    Cache key to invalidate.

Returns:
    - 0 on success
    - 1 on failure

UTILITIES
=========

$Function STRING .version(VOID)

Get the VMOD version string.

Returns the version in format "major.minor.patch".

$Function INT .ping(VOID)

Check if the RGW backend is available.

Returns:
    - 0 if RGW is unavailable
    - 1 if RGW is available

ERROR HANDLING
==============

On error, the VMOD functions will log appropriate error messages
to the VSL (Varnish Shared Log) and return sensible default values.
